# Letter card system

Recent architecture: **two atlases + runtime tint** (not monolithic `JumbalayaDeck.png`).

| Asset | Atlas name | Role |
|-------|------------|------|
| `JumbalayaLetters.png` | `letters` | 13×2 glyph grid (A–M row 0, N–Z row 1), white letters |
| `JumbalayaCardFrame.png` | `letter_frame` | White silhouette; tinted at draw time |

Cell size: **71×95** logical px (142×190 at 2x). Paths: `resources/textures/{1x,2x}/`.

## Key modules

- `letter_card_faces.lua` — `glyph_pos`, `fill_color`, `draw_composite`
- `card_visuals.lua` — `set_sprites`, `draw_front`; frame on `children.center`, glyph on `children.front`
- `letter_card_palette.lua` — color key → RGBA (`red`, `black`, `modified`)
- `deck_face_colors.lua` — source RGBA data (regenerated by build tool)
- `definitions.lua` — `G.P_CARDS` (`red_A`…`modified_Z`), `G.P_CENTERS.letter_base`
- `assets.lua` — registers atlases in `Game:set_render_settings()`

## Color keys

- `red` — default face (`DEFAULT_FACE_COLOR`)
- `black` — alternate deck color
- `modified` — perk/modified cards (`MODIFIED_FACE_COLOR`)

## Change chain

When altering letter cards, touch the full pipeline as needed:

1. `_tools/build_letter_atlas.py` → PNGs + `deck_face_colors.lua`
2. `app/startup/assets.lua` atlas spec
3. `word_game/model/cards/definitions.lua`
4. `letter_card_faces.lua` / `card_visuals.lua` / `letter_tile.lua`
5. `tests/unit/test_letter_card_faces.lua`

Source art for rebuild: `assets/JumbalayaDeck.jpg` or legacy deck PNG grid.
